import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 537 | Historical-Reversal Simulation | Perfect World — The Broken Generation From Shi Hao's Absence","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 537 | Historical-Reversal Simulation | Perfect World — The Broken Generation From Shi Hao's Absence","no":537,"module":3,"tags":["Historical-Reversal Simulation","Perfect World","Protagonist Absence","Civilizational Generation Break","Quest-Domain Simulation Review"],"related":["84-Archaeology Protocol General Outline","87-Knowledge-Only Return Principle","05-Myriad-Ranks Joint-Advancement Basic Program","49-Governance Framework and Power Checks"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0537_模块3-历史倒车模拟-完美世界-石昊缺位断代.md","filePath":"en/0537_模块3-历史倒车模拟-完美世界-石昊缺位断代.md"}`),a={name:"en/0537_模块3-历史倒车模拟-完美世界-石昊缺位断代.md"};function r(s,e,l,h,c,d){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-537-historical-reversal-simulation-perfect-world-—-the-broken-generation-from-shi-hao-s-absence" tabindex="-1">Entry 537 | Historical-Reversal Simulation | Perfect World — The Broken Generation From Shi Hao&#39;s Absence <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-537-historical-reversal-simulation-perfect-world-—-the-broken-generation-from-shi-hao-s-absence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 537 | Historical-Reversal Simulation | Perfect World — The Broken Generation From Shi Hao&#39;s Absence&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain Civilizational-Experience System | Benchmark base: Documents 84, 87, 05, 49</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-the-only-shield-is-gone-who-shields-all-beings-from-the-wind" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when the only shield is gone, who shields all beings from the wind <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-the-only-shield-is-gone-who-shields-all-beings-from-the-wind" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when the only shield is gone, who shields all beings from the wind&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Perfect World&#39;s time tension concentrates on one point: a Shi-Hao-style Youth Supreme all alone fights through the ages, alone carries the darkness, alone faces the final boss — almost the entire civilization&#39;s only &quot;wind shield.&quot; The stronger he grows, the more civilization ties its fate to him alone. What reversal simulation must deduce is a cold and necessary hypothesis — <strong>if Shi Hao at a key node is absent (falls, is blocked, arrives too late), along which direction does the world slide on the time axis?</strong> This is no disrespect to heroes, but the strictest engineering test of &quot;protagonist-uniqueness dependence.&quot;</p><p>Six top-level axioms are the review&#39;s highest criteria: anti-predation axiom requires civilization not buy peace via &quot;one person devouring all enemies&quot;; republican axiom of Myriad Races requires billions&#39; fate not bet on one youth; collective ascension axiom precisely points out a hero&#39;s highest virtue should be &quot;carrying Myriad Ranks forward,&quot; not bearing everything alone; causal self-discipline axiom constrains the deduction to run only in Quest-Sediment-Domain sandboxes, only knowledge returned without perturbing real planes; law-first axiom requires the &quot;absence — generation break — reversal&quot; causal chain deduced first by law, not plot-driven last-minute rescue. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-hidden-costs-of-the-youth-supreme-mode" tabindex="-1">I. Hidden Costs of the Youth-Supreme Mode <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-hidden-costs-of-the-youth-supreme-mode" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Hidden Costs of the Youth-Supreme Mode&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The sandbox first restores the structural cost of the &quot;Shi Hao mode.&quot; It is short-term immensely effective: a heaven-defying talent grows far faster than peers, alone resolving crises civilization collectively cannot handle. But long-term buries three hidden dangers:</p><ol><li><strong>Collective capability atrophy</strong>: since the strongest backstops, each race and domain no longer seriously builds its own defense and governance; capability quietly atrophies in dependence.</li><li><strong>Knowledge personalization</strong>: the highest cognition the protagonist gains along his path is mostly scattered with his movement trail, not openly and systematically retained; once he is absent, civilization&#39;s collective cognitive height falls accordingly.</li><li><strong>Governance hollowing</strong>: the true four-power checks of deliberative, executive, judicial, supervisory (Document 49) are long-term de facto hollowed by &quot;the protagonist has the final say&quot;; institutional muscles atrophy.</li></ol><h2 id="ii-the-three-act-curve-of-absence-generation-break" tabindex="-1">II. The Three-Act Curve of Absence-Generation-Break <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-three-act-curve-of-absence-generation-break" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Three-Act Curve of Absence-Generation-Break&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The sandbox deduces the script &quot;Shi Hao absent before some final battle&quot;; the reversal curve has three acts:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Act</th><th>Stage</th><th>Reversal Signs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Act I</td><td>Crisis at hand, no one can stop it</td><td>Dark army presses; each race discovers itself long out of practice</td></tr><tr><td>Act II</td><td>Hasty patchwork, each fights alone</td><td>Races resist by instinct; no unified command; retreat steadily</td></tr><tr><td>Act III</td><td>Civilization generation-breaks backward</td><td>Survivors fall back; generations later even &quot;there once was a Youth Supreme&quot; becomes legend</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Most worth reviewing is the <strong>dependence-inertia period</strong> between Act I and Act II: even when everyone realizes the protagonist is absent, in the short term they cannot organize, because collective coordination ability long ago atrophied in &quot;waiting for the protagonist.&quot; This is precisely the &quot;high dependence&quot; time cost in protagonist-uniqueness dependence judgment.</p><h2 id="iii-control-experiment-if-the-collective-had-been-lifted" tabindex="-1">III. Control Experiment: If the Collective Had Been Lifted <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-control-experiment-if-the-collective-had-been-lifted" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Control Experiment: If the Collective Had Been Lifted&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The sandbox ran a key control: replace &quot;the protagonist alone bears everything&quot; with &quot;the protagonist leads, Myriad Ranks republican co-build, Alaya Network synchronously retains cognition&quot;; other crises unchanged. Result:</p><ul><li>The protagonist may still charge as strongest combat, but each race under the symbiotic system long ago had its own defense and command network;</li><li>The protagonist&#39;s insights along the way uploaded in real time to Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision; civilization&#39;s collective always shares his cognitive height;</li><li>Even if the protagonist is temporarily absent, the four-power checks governance machine runs as usual; civilization does not collapse.</li></ul><p>The control proves: <strong>a hero&#39;s value is not in bearing everything alone, but in lifting the collective to his shoulder height.</strong> This is precisely the collective ascension axiom&#39;s precise expression in the time dimension.</p><h2 id="iv-review-results-three-de-dependence-patches" tabindex="-1">IV. Review Results: Three De-Dependence Patches <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-review-results-three-de-dependence-patches" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Review Results: Three De-Dependence Patches&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Distribute defense</strong>: civilization may not pin national defense on a single strong one; each race must have a symbiotic co-built distributed defense network.</li><li><strong>Network cognition</strong>: any strong one&#39;s highest cognition must in real time be openly retained on the Alaya Network; eliminate &quot;person absent, Dao absent too.&quot;</li><li><strong>Normalize governance</strong>: deliberative, executive, judicial, supervisory four powers must run normally; may not be hollowed just because a strong person is nearby.</li></ul><p>All three patches come from isolated sandboxes, following the &quot;Knowledge-Only Return Principle,&quot; already filed as Civilizational Correction Engineering experience.</p><p>Another control worth noting in the sandbox: when a Shi-Hao-style hero uploads insights in real time to the Alaya Network, even if he is temporarily absent in a battle, each race can organize resistance on its own using openly retained cognition; losses drop sharply. This shows between &quot;the strong alone bears&quot; and &quot;the strong leads and lifts,&quot; the difference is not power, but willingness to turn oneself into a public inherit-the collective can inherit. A hero&#39;s highest loyalty is not dying for all beings, but making all beings not need him alone.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: pressing all civilization&#39;s fate on one person is the greatest waste of billions&#39; evolutionary potential — they could have been lifted into main force, but were raised into audience</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: alone devouring all enemies looks heroic, but actually lets civilization collectively lose the chance to grow its own fangs</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: the Shi Hao mode is more heroic, more tragic than Tang Luo&#39;s bounty system, but still &quot;high protagonist dependence&quot;; Heng Yuan Zhou wants &quot;network-style&quot; — extremely low dependence, everyone can fight</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the review registers each race sacrificed in the absence script, proving Myriad-Rank republicanism is not the weak&#39;s comfort, but civilization&#39;s bulletproof vest</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: absence-generation-break curve, three de-dependence patches openly filed, for all planes with hero-worship traditions to self-check</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Perfect World&#39;s reversal simulation does not deny heroes, but loosens the hero&#39;s bonds. A truly great Youth Supreme should not be civilization&#39;s only wind shield — he should be the person who bricks the whole shield into billions&#39; bones. The Shi-Hao-absence sandbox reminds all civilizations: prosperity that pins fate on one person is always borrowed prosperity; when due, it returns principal plus interest to the origin.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./84-考古协议总纲.html">84-Archaeology Protocol General Outline</a> · <a href="./87-仅回传知识原则.html">87-Knowledge-Only Return Principle</a> · <a href="./05-万族共进基本纲领.html">05-Myriad-Ranks Joint-Advancement Basic Program</a> · <a href="./49-治理框架与权力制衡.html">49-Governance Framework and Power Checks</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',26)])])}const p=t(a,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
